<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm8a-wenchang ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 8A (unknown payload, Wenchang Commercial LC-1) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
NO public LM-8A time/altitude/velocity table found. Loft: SURROGATE — LM-3B typical GTO trajectory, CALT &#x27;LM-3A Series Launch Vehicles User&#x27;s Manual&#x27; Issue 2011, Tables 3-5/3-6
(event time s, flight altitude km, ground range km), liftoff altitude 1.8 km removed. Cut at Stage-3 first shutdown T+615.7 s, 204.3 km, 2466.2 km.
Source: http://www.georing.biz/usefull/LM-3A%20Series%20Launch%20Vehicles%20User&#x27;s%20Manual%20Issue%202011.pdf
Ground range IS published, so no Rel.Vel split is needed; velocities are d/dt of interpolated alt/range (rel_vel = |v| ground-relative).
One horizontal assumption: LM-3B&#x27;s published ground range is laid along this mission&#x27;s constant-azimuth rhumb (LM-3B itself doglegs).
Az 140.4 deg = initial bearing pad -&gt; NAVAREA XI 26-0481 zone B/C centroid (~7.7N 120.6E, Sulu Sea), issued 23 Oct 2026;
zone A (~13.05N 116.48E) bears 140.1 deg (consistent). Replaces earlier ~127 deg guess. Source: https://www.sealagom.com/navarea/11/message/25242/
Not flown yet: T0 = LL2 NET 2026-10-25T01:50Z (window 01:42-02:32Z per NOTAMs).
Pad (LL2): 19.597275N 110.930753E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=140.36 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-10-25T01:50:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
<Placemark><name>Pad (lm8a-wenchang)</name><Point><coordinates>110.9307530,19.5972750,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
